.TH FANCTL 1 "2026" "acer-predator-ph315-51-fan-control" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fanctl \- control the Acer Predator PH315-51 fan mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fanctl
[\fIstatus\fR|\fIfull\fR|\fIauto\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fanctl
is an unprivileged client for
.BR fanctld (8),
a root daemon that writes the Acer Predator PH315-51 embedded
controller's fan registers directly. It talks to the daemon over the
Unix socket
.IR /run/fanctld.sock ,
which is restricted by filesystem permissions to one local user.
.PP
Without arguments,
.B fanctl
behaves as if
.I status
was given.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the daemon's current fan mode as JSON: \fB{"ok": true, "mode": "auto"}\fR.
.TP
.B full
Force both fans to maximum speed.
.TP
.B auto
Return fan control to the vendor's own curve.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B fanctl
exits 0 on success, 1 if the daemon could not be reached or returned
an error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/fanctld.sock
The daemon's Unix socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fanctld (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Yaroslav Yushchenko
